@prefix dhc:   <https://digitalhome.cloud/ontology#> .
@prefix brick: <https://brickschema.org/schema/Brick#> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/> .

# A battery declaring no dhc:governedBy.
#
# Rejected by nfc15100-2024:ESSGovernanceShape (⚠ illustrative rule: 2024
# brings energy storage into the scope of NF C 15-100).
#
# Under 2015 this same file conforms — not because it is fine, but because NO
# SHAPE TARGETS A BATTERY at all. That is the coverage-vs-compliance trap this
# repo keeps paying for: SHACL reports only failures, so "out of scope" and
# "checked and clean" are the same silence. The viewer draws the difference as
# transparency; here the test asserts it directly, so the 2015 pass is recorded
# as an absence of rules rather than mistaken for approval.
ex:fr-ess-ungoverned a brick:Battery .
